Z||000000||Matthew_Fiero||10-07-2001||05:12 PM||||hey Voytek, you sent me this message a while ago "The slave doesn't come with any lines - that's ordered separately.<BR>Are you ordering the front-to-back clutch line? They're a B*TCH to bend and install (I broke one). You're better off installing a flexible steel braided line. That's what I have and installation was a breeze.<P>I had it custom made at a Big Rig shop - those guys have all the means. If you have the old line, just cut off the ends / fittings and ask them to incorporate them into the steel braided line. Make sure it's really close with the diameter (doesn't have to be 100% same size).<P>The dealership wanted $220 CDN for a replacement line. I had this one custom made for $80. It took the guy 1 hour to make. Good luck."<P>i am interested to know more about this, can you msn me at breather60@hotmail.com or ICQ 25132956<BR>i just need to ask a couple of things, i would have PM'ed you but a lot of people don't check their PM's for weeks<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Matthew_Fiero (edited 10-08-2001).]||||reg||1
